{
  "_comment": [
    "T3.11.07 — how money moves when it moves OUTSIDE the platform.",
    "",
    "There are two settlement models, not three: on the platform, or off it.",
    "Cash is not a peer of «transfer» — it is one of the systems people settle",
    "in outside the platform, alongside a bank app, a remittance service or a",
    "stablecoin. That is why `cash` is the first entry in `global` and not a",
    "model of its own.",
    "",
    "`global` is offered everywhere; `countries` adds what works in one place.",
    "Payment is between two people who may be in different countries, so the",
    "form offers the systems of BOTH ends of the route plus the global set.",
    "",
    "Seeded from our own corpus and from the corridors we serve, not imported",
    "from anyone else's catalogue. Our 15 128-message analysis names almost",
    "nothing here — «наличные» 96, USDT 23, everything else at or near zero —",
    "so breadth is a bet on the market we want, not a description of the one we",
    "measured. Free text stays in the form for exactly that reason: a list this",
    "young must not be able to tell a carrier they are wrong."
  ],
